from the precheck's PRE-LOAD MANIFEST — that threading happens at these callers"],"finding":"The File impact inventory for the completion-sidecar enrichment omits the two PASS/FAIL close-time emit call sites — src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py (completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, ...) at :405, reached for both PASS and FAIL via _emit_completion_sidecar) and src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (standalone emit(..., material=None) at :240). Both are the sites where the FAIL/PASS COMPLETION_VERDICT is emitted with material=None; the fingerprint inputs named by the fix plan (completion_read_basis, receipt_digest, completion_prefetch_manifest) originate at these callers and must be threaded in — enriching build_payload/emit alone leaves these two paths still writing material=None.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc8da04a9468943d4","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan → 'File impact:' list (and Problem statement quoting close_precheck.py:405)","norm_id":"nad00d0b91a7a35a3","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["close_precheck.py:405 left unedited → the close-time PASS/FAIL COMPLETION_VERDICT still emits with material=None, so AC1 (PASS and FAIL carry a fingerprint) silently under-delivers on the primary close path","transition_close.py:240 left unedited → the standalone certify path still emits material=None, leaving a second unpinned emitter that AC1's regression test (which asserts a FAIL carries a non-null fingerprint) may not exercise"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend File impact with close_precheck.py and transition_close.py, and state the parameter path by which _emit_completion_sidecar/emit receive the pinned material argument (rather than material=None) so both PASS and FAIL close-time sidecars carry the fingerprint.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_acc